//   6 STATS     the registered verdict in every branch (eleven parts).   7 LINES  the twelve bottom lines.   8 CHECKS  twelve rows; a failed check says NOT WEIGHED.   9 REPORT   tables and lines.   10 SOURCE  the ids appear once; no clock, random or file.
// SABOTAGE LOG (195 mutants of tools/ship/headToHead26.mjs, each alone in its own worktree copy): 170 went red by name on the first pass. 25 went 0 red; 15 got a row (or a re-aimed pattern) and went red on the second run: a 964-weight vector in wip, a champion, a search or the start (the length test was `>=`); the first candidate flown as the start ROUNDED TO FLOAT32 (a start of 0.1 in every weight); armsOf without its every-champion check (the first pattern left a dangling `||` and was a syntax error, exit 1 with no FAIL line; re-aimed); the audit keeping the fixture-record's `fixture` and `start` (both patterns had matched the doc comment and were re-aimed at the return line); startOf's train and held-out ranges (a score that differs by range) and its default seconds; the extra-power line's MEAN of the dark and lit extra kW, the audit line's DARK power, the reported line's change from wip's and its lit gain (a champion whose dark and lit differ); a non-array champion record (null, a string, an object that looks like a list); Wip's sum of squares held alone (two weights moved by +0.5 and -0.5 and by +1e-5 and -1e-5, so the sum is unchanged and the sum of squares is not).
//   TEN ARE DECLARED EQUIVALENT: (a) the last digit of Wip's sum in the fingerprint constant (the changed literal parses to the same double); (b) `=== 1` against `>= 1` in championOf's seed count and (c) in the TWELVE SEARCHES check (with the registered count of rows and every registered seed present at least once, each is present exactly once); (d) `>` against `>=` at a mean dark thrust of exactly 0.9 (0.9 is not representable and a mean of equal values rarely lands on it; tested a hair either side at 0.901 and 0.899); (e) dropping `Number.isFinite(fx.at02)` and (f) `Number.isFinite(fx.at0)` (a NaN there makes `===` or the difference test false anyway); (g) dropping disjoint(TRAIN, HELD) from the id-sets check (two constants of the file); (h) `>=` against `===` when comparing a champion's held-out value with the group's maximum (the maximum is one of the values); (i) dropping `rowsOf(au, g).length > 0 &&` before `.some(...)` (an empty group matches no row anyway); (j) dropping `isW(w)` from the champion check (a champion equal to a stored search of 963 finite weights is itself 963 finite weights, and the other check demands every search be).
// NOT CHECKED, said plainly: that 600 iterations move a 963-weight network far from its start (that is what the round measures); that the three champions are comparable across prices (each is the best of four on 40 held-out ids at its own price, and H22 showed that ranking to be a noisy selector).
